    <text type="letter">
        <body>
            <div type="writingSession">
                <pb n="1"/>
                <opener><dateline><date when="1948-06-25">25 June 1948</date>.</dateline>AG 300.4
                    L-6-G-549<lb/>SUBJECT: Orders<lb/>TO: <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928"
                        type="person">PROF PAUL TILLICH</rs> (US Citizen, Consultant)<lb/>Temporary
                    Employee OMGUS</opener>
                <p>1. <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">PROF PAUL TILLICH</rs> is
                    invited to proceed from <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__319" type="place">New
                        York</rs>, <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__684" type="place">USA</rs> o/a <date
                        when="1948-07-20">20 July 1948</date> to <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__143"
                        type="place">Frankfurt</rs> and <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__279"
                        type="place">Marburg</rs>, <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__122" type="place"
                        >Germany</rs> for a persiod of approximately twenty-seven (27) days, for the
                    purpose of lecturing at <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__279" type="place"
                        >Marburg</rs> University. Upon compl ret to proper sta.</p>
                <p>2. The travel directed herein has been cleared in accordance with Par 11, Cir 28,
                    Hq <unclear>EUCOM</unclear>, <date when="1947-05-09">9 May 47</date>.</p>
                <p>3. <hi rend="u">All cost of travel outside of <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__122"
                            type="place">Germany</rs> will be borne by the indiv concerned.</hi></p>
                <p>4. All cost of travel within <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__122" type="place"
                        >Germany</rs>, US Zone and <hi rend="u">US Sector of <rs
                            ref="#tillich_place_id__37" type="place">Berlin</rs></hi> will be
                    chargeable to the Dept of the Army.</p>
                <p>5. No per diem or reinbursement for travel is <choice>
                        <abbr>atzd</abbr>
                        <expan>authorized</expan>
                    </choice>.</p>
                <p>6. Travel by military aircraft, government motor vehicle and/or rail is atzd.
                    RTA&apos;s issued for rail travel for personnel within <rs
                        ref="#tillich_place_id__122" type="place">Germany</rs> will be chargeable
                    ¿¿¿ (TDN. 2180425 G 801-2 G432-02 99-999).</p>
                <p>7. This order is authorization for American Entry Permit Officer to issue entry
                    permit into <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__122" type="place">Germany</rs> with
                    facilities.</p>
                <p>8. Auth: Par 10a, Cir 28, Hq EUCOM, <date when="1947-05-09">9 May 47</date> as
                    amended by Sec IV, Cir 91, Hq EUCOM, <date when="1947-11-08">8 Nov 47</date> and
                    Sec II, Sec III and Sec IV of Cir 57, Hq EUCOM, <date when="1947-07-23">23 July
                        47</date> as amended by Sec III, Cir 91, Hq EUCOM, <date when="1947-11-08">8
                        Nov 47</date>.</p>
                <p>BY COMMAND OF <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__5150" type="person">MAJOR GENERAL
                        HAYS</rs><lb/><figure>
                        <figDesc>[Stempel: <q>OFFICE OF MILITARY GOVERNMENT FOR <rs
                                    ref="#tillich_place_id__122" type="place">GERMANY</rs> (U. S.)
                                OFFICIAL</q>]</figDesc>
                    </figure></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rend="hand"><rs ref="#tillich_place_id__5149" type="person">JB
                                Mallon</rs></hi><lb/><rs ref="#tillich_place_id__5149" type="person"
                                ><unclear>J.</unclear> B. Mallon</rs><lb/><unclear>Officer</unclear>
                        AGD<lb/>Asst Adjutant General</signed>
                    <hi rend="u">DISTRIBUTION:</hi><lb/>25 – Indiv concerned<lb/>1 – AG
                    Records<lb/>1 – M/R Sec<lb/>1 – E &amp; CR Div </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
